{"id": "EUVD-2026-81742", "enisaUuid": "33e73c13-cf3f-37c4-bcb1-c1e690b24a16", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSv4/flexfiles: fix NULL dereference for NFSv4.0 data servers\n\nflexfiles accepts NFSv4.0 data servers, but two NFSv4 code paths assume\nthe data server client has a session. Unlike NFSv4.1+, an NFSv4.0 client\nhas no session (clp->cl_session is NULL; it uses clp->cl_slot_tbl), so\nI/O to a v4.0 flexfiles DS oopses:\n\n  - nfs4_init_ds_session() dereferences clp->cl_session->session_state\n    while seeding the DS lease. It also only seeds cl_lease_time when\n    NFS4_SESSION_INITING is set; without a session that never happens, so\n    cl_lease_time stays 0 and nfs4_renew_state() busy-loops, requeuing\n    every 5 seconds. Seed the lease whenever there is no session and\n    return before touching session state.\n\n  - ff_layout_async_handle_error_v4() dereferences\n    clp->cl_session->fc_slot_table on every DS I/O error. Fall back to the\n    v4.0 transport slot table (clp->cl_slot_tbl) when there is no session.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:06", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/336b6da10021c69a8f273bbacdf7432fdc89a06f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5527af72b0100c94287bfec901b6313eeac567ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/163c16e01f53fc8eb8d0f3484ae6c382265ecbbd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/436a214514e24103159aea455147d58b44a8a585", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b03ebbf8d5e8f6af4ecd6c65375232dd1ec32cc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90149", "GHSA-5pv5-p9q3-rvv6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.61, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0350a64c-a841-395d-97c4-4be71e46d1bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.12"}, {"id": "098b093b-b04c-3205-8133-71fc22fdb138", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1d0428d1-63d4-3382-a880-0970636cdc3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7878ca140084ec267ede48fce64d7e60f6d873e <336b6da10021c69a8f273bbacdf7432fdc89a06f"}, {"id": "1d884241-3225-391a-b84d-6e6a434d237e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "5045eb68-e8ac-35d8-96fe-15deda4e942c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7878ca140084ec267ede48fce64d7e60f6d873e <2b03ebbf8d5e8f6af4ecd6c65375232dd1ec32cc"}, {"id": "6b3eeee3-723e-3bc7-8794-22d22984e79d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "8ce85029-c5f6-3986-99ed-66586cd45d42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7878ca140084ec267ede48fce64d7e60f6d873e <436a214514e24103159aea455147d58b44a8a585"}, {"id": "bc800108-f0e1-3002-91e0-89e2789a50ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7878ca140084ec267ede48fce64d7e60f6d873e <5527af72b0100c94287bfec901b6313eeac567ca"}, {"id": "c9636175-f33c-3627-a887-a031cfaad129", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "ce3060dc-d170-31ca-bee9-a439f96955cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d200d218-1e69-371f-a5fc-5a635d74493c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7878ca140084ec267ede48fce64d7e60f6d873e <163c16e01f53fc8eb8d0f3484ae6c382265ecbbd"}, {"id": "d83b057e-892b-3017-a7c4-cf1d1f089d90", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b984b9c3-5fad-3fca-b4b0-da973bba489a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}